\title{meteogal2fdata: MeteoGalicia observations and functional data}
\description{
Download and read daily observations from the MeteoGalicia automatic
station network, keeping the validation code of every measurement, and
convert them to \code{fda.usc::fdata} and \code{fda.usc::ldata} objects with one
365-point curve per station-year. Only base R, 'jsonlite' (to parse the
JSON responses) and 'fda.usc' are used.
}
\details{
Workflow: \code{\link[=meteogal2inventory]{meteogal2inventory()}} (stations) -> \code{\link[=meteogal2download]{meteogal2download()}}
(raw station-year files with codes and a provenance manifest) ->
\code{\link[=meteogal2df]{meteogal2df()}} (daily data.frame, quality chosen with \code{quality}) ->
\code{\link[=meteogal2fdata]{meteogal2fdata()}} / \code{\link[=meteogal2lfdata]{meteogal2lfdata()}} (functional data). The codes are
described by \code{\link[=meteogal_qc_codes]{meteogal_qc_codes()}}.
}
